{
  "index": 9,
  "response": "\nTo find the x-intercept of the equation y = 2x + 4, we need to set the value of y equal to 0 and solve for x.\n\nSo, we can write:\n\n2x + 4 = 0\n\nNow, we can subtract 4 from both sides of the equation to get:\n\n2x = -4\n\nNext, we can divide both sides of the equation by 2 to get:\n\nx = -4/2\n\nTherefore, the x-intercept of the equation y = 2x + 4 is x = -2.",
